# AI naming and brand mark

The AI assistant in this product is called **Edify**. Never use the name **Quinn**
in any user-facing copy, prop names, component names, ARIA labels, or comments
on new code.

This decision overrides any legacy naming you find in the codebase. Existing
`Quinn*` components and references will be renamed in a separate sweep — do
not introduce new ones, and when you touch an old surface for an unrelated
change, prefer "Edify" in any user-facing string you touch.

## Logo / mark

Anywhere the AI shows up — provenance chip, avatar, "the AI is thinking"
affordance, **a value or row the AI suggested, selected, or pre-filled**,
"agent picked these" callouts, AI-pulled imports, etc. — use the existing
`EdifyMark` component. Never the lucide `Sparkles` icon.

Rule of thumb: **if the icon is signalling "the AI did this", it must be
`EdifyMark`.** Reach for `Sparkles` only for non-AI ornament (e.g. a generic
"new" sparkle on a marketing surface), and even then prefer something else.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Sparkles icon + "Quinn" copy
import { Sparkles } from 'lucide-react';

<span style={{ color: 'var(--color-accent-quinn)' }}>
  <Sparkles size={12} /> Quinn
</span>

// ✅ GOOD — EdifyMark + "Edify" copy
import EdifyMark from '@/components/EdifyMark/EdifyMark';

<span style={{ color: 'var(--color-text-secondary)' }}>
  <EdifyMark size={12} /> Edify
</span>

// ✅ GOOD — AI pre-selected a value
<EdifyMark size={14} color="var(--color-accent-mid, #28AFC9)" />
I pre-selected the 12 coffee recipes on your menu.
```

`EdifyMark` is a drop-in lucide-shaped component — same `size`, `color`, and
pass-through SVG props, so you can swap it for `Sparkles` without touching
the surrounding markup.

## User-facing copy

| ❌ Don't write              | ✅ Write instead             |
|----------------------------|------------------------------|
| "Ask Quinn"                | "Ask Edify"                  |
| "Quinn updated this"       | "Edify updated this"         |
| "Quinn is thinking…"       | "Edify is thinking…"         |
| `aria-label="Quinn"`        | `aria-label="Edify"`          |

## Comments and identifiers

For new files: name components, props, IDs, and CSS variables `edify*` /
`Edify*` — not `quinn*` / `Quinn*`. In existing files where renaming the
symbol would cascade widely, leave the identifier alone but match the
surrounding code's voice in comments (use "Edify" in new sentences).

## When you can keep "Quinn"

- Historical references in `DESIGN-RATIONALE.md`, transcripts, or other
  artefacts that capture a past state of the product.
- Identifiers in deep legacy modules where a localised rename would touch
  dozens of unrelated files (do not introduce new ones).
